Here's the final picture, end to end:

```
Manual Trigger
    ↓
Fetch PO Data (Mock)          ← hard-codes PO-2026-00847 / Acme Supplies Ltd. / $14,750
    ↓
PO Review [HITL — High]       ← reviewer sees PO#, Vendor, Amount; enters optional Notes
    ↓
Approved?
    ↓ true                    ↓ false
Log Approval                  PO Rejected (End)
    ↓
PO Approved (End)
```

**Log Approval** assembles a single confirmation string — `"PO approved: PO-2026-00847 | Vendor: Acme Supplies Ltd. | Amount: 14750 | Notes: …"` — and returns it as `logApproval1.output.message`. When you connect a real logging system later (Orchestrator queue, email, database write), you just replace this node and use that same message field.

